{"method":"The shape of beautiful real faces: per-vertex offsets on the canonical face mesh, fitted so that the rendered face, read by MediaPipe's face landmarker exactly as the photographs were, matches the average of public-domain portraits of film stars, by sex.\n\n- the photographs: one a person, of that person alone (no second face over a third of its width), the most frontal with |yaw| <= 22 deg, the face at least 140 px wide;\n- only closed, unsmiling mouths and open eyes looking ahead (a smile narrows the eyes and lifts the cheeks; closed or squinting eyes were left out), adults only;\n- each face frontalised by the inverse of its head rotation, centred on the midpoint of the two eyes' centres (the middle of each eye's corners, so gaze does not move it), scaled to put them one unit apart and levelled; averaged per sex;\n- the fit: render the face (no makeup, hair off the face), measure it the same way, move the vertices by half the remaining difference (x and y; depth is set by the form step), symmetrised and smoothed over about 4 mm, landmarks that do not respond left alone; repeated, the best iteration kept (root-mean-square residual 1.07 mm for women, 1.82 mm for men);\n- the lid margins and the inner lip line are left out (photographs read the lids by lash lines and liner, and the lips' closure is not a shape): the face places the lids on the iris by measured margin-to-reflex distances and the mouth's corners at the height measured on the same photographs.","female":{"n":29,"closedMouths":29,"offsets":[[-0.0,-0.47,0.0],[0.0,1.623,0.0],[-0.0,-0.811,0.0],[0.243,-0.261,0.0],[-0.0,1.295,0.0],[-0.0,0.547,0.0],[0.0,-0.849,0.0],[0.781,0.228,0.0],[-0.0,-2.663,0.0],[-0.0,-2.836,0.0],[-0.0,6.765,0.0],[-0.0,-0.392,0.0],[-0.0,-0.364,0.0],[-0.0,-0.291,0.0],[-0.0,-0.334,0.0],[-0.0,-0.408,0.0],[-0.0,-0.527,0.0],[-0.0,-0.64,0.0],[-0.0,1.074,0.0],[0.0,1.37,0.0],[0.418,0.429,0.0],[-1.809,1.171,0.0],[0.721,0.876,0.0],[0.94,0.874,0.0],[0.997,0.575,0.0],[0.997,0.205,0.0],[0.